/P 92 0 R
/E (If possible, you might even try and practice how to get out safely. This could include seeking help from your siblings or friends, should they come to visit. Before taking any measures, however, always make sure that your safety and the safety of those around you is ensured. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Always document any abusive behavior that you witness or experience. This can help you in building a legal case against your abuser\(s\), to get custody for your children or even to simply apply for protection in a court of law. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (You can document your case by \(1\) taking pictures of physical evidence of violence \(such as any scars or marks on your face or parts of your body\); \(2\) by secretly recording conversations \(be they on the phone or face-to-face\) that may prove the abuse; \(3\) recording video evidence of the abuse; such as if the abuser is being violent with you, or any other member of the house or with a pet; \(4\) pictures of the house or room in disarray after a violent episode; and \(5\) any pictures of possible weapons \(such as a knife or a gun\) via which the abuser threatened to hurt you or someone you love. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (You could also keep a diary in which you record the different instances of abuse that take place at different times \(both outside and within the home\). Record the time, date and event with clarity. Include the names of any witnesses present that may be seen the abuse.    . )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
