/E (If possible, try and keep all weapons \(including guns and knives\) and other objects that might be used to hurt you locked up and out of easy access. If you live with other people in the house \(such as in a joint family system\) where they may try and assist the abuser in hurting you, then be very careful to steer clear from any objects that might be used for the same purpose. If you need to, get a hold of a similar object to defend yourself. But make sure you and your children are safe at all times. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
